Package: cybroid-edition-engineering
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: all
Maintainer: CybroidOS maintainers <citos@cybroid.com>
Homepage: https://cybroid.com/cybroidos
Section: metapackages
Priority: optional
Depends: cybroid-plasma (>= @VERSION@), kicad, kicad-symbols, kicad-footprints, freecad, librecad, openscad, ngspice, simulide, fritzing, gtkwave, iverilog, ghdl, pulseview, sigrok, arduino, avrdude, esptool, openocd, picocom, python3-serial, octave, octave-control, octave-signal, python3-numpy, python3-scipy, python3-matplotlib, python3-sympy, python3-pandas, jupyterlab
Description: CybroidOS Engineering: for electronics, CAD and science
 Design, simulation, hardware and analysis: KiCad with its symbol and
 footprint libraries, FreeCAD, LibreCAD and OpenSCAD; ngspice, SimulIDE
 and Fritzing for circuits; Icarus Verilog, GHDL and GTKWave for digital
 logic; PulseView for logic analysers; the Arduino IDE, avrdude, esptool
 and OpenOCD for boards; GNU Octave with its control and signal packages;
 and Python with NumPy, SciPy, SymPy, pandas and Matplotlib in JupyterLab.
 Arduino IDE 2 installs from the App Centre.
 .
 The same CybroidOS as every edition (look, updates, Hangar), with these
 tools added. An installed CybroidOS becomes this edition by installing this
 package; several editions can be installed together.
